    "body": "Yeah, I noticed this divergence. As part of this change let's get implementers to sign off on aligning the task sources used. In practice task sources are very hard to observe so this should be fine.\r\n\r\nActually it looks like both Chromium and WebKit already use DOM manipulation for popover. So this is just a fix where the current spec is bad:\r\n\r\n- [WebKit](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/346fdad1569da1c50564a62ee569a7f519d9cd46/Source/WebCore/html/HTMLDetailsElement.cpp#L139)\r\n- [Chromium](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/html_element.cc;l=1609;drc=acd0e1034f101c2ef8bafa49186bcb84e550dc27;bpv=1;bpt=1)\r\n\r\nAnd I think using DOM manipulation is best anyway, since the flow is generally `something happens in DOM -> fire the event`, which is sometimes derived from `user interaction -> something happens in DOM` but sometimes not.",
